Texture cache descriptor tables: lazy invalidation, power-of-two growth, resolved ids in an array.
(ProsperoEden eglantine-a42b4d4-ps5.d 0017 descriptor-table-lazy, from zortos293/Eglantine
5bef7354b4, upstream PRs #256/#277.)

Invalidate only marks the table and the next Read clears the read bits once, instead of every
deleted image clearing both tables of every channel; tables grow by powers of two instead of
rounding up to 0x80000 entries (16 MiB each); the resolved image view and sampler ids live in an
array beside the descriptors instead of hash maps keyed by index. EglantinePS5's opt-in
validation walk (EDEN_NX2_TC_CORRUPT_IDS=1) now poisons those arrays.

